{"text": "INBIFO Institut far biologische Forschung GmbH - Koin CONFIDENTIAL\n{4 May.2002 _ C\\Documents and Settings\\buggiLocal Settings\\Temporary Internet\nFiles\\OLK24\\CONCEPT.DOC Page t\n\n\u2014_\u2014_\u2014\u2014$\u2014\u2014\nNOTE\n\nDATE: 12 April 2002\nFROM: wsT\nTo: WRE, HHM, ERO, HSA, PSN, EAN, PMT, EEM, PMV, FRK, WOC\n\nSUBJECT: _ B7031 Study Concept \u201cAcute Inhalation Assay to Quickly Detect\nCigarette Modifications with Regard to Sensory Irritation and\nSystemic Toxicity\u201d (WSA project 1369)\n\nce: -\n\nObjectives: The objective of this series of acute inhalation studies is to quickly\ninvestigate cigarette modifications with regard to\n* sensory irritation as marker for irritation for guidance purpose and\n\u00a9 acute systemic toxicity as a safety screen.\n\nRequirements to the inhalation assay\n\u00a9 Easy to perform\n\u00a9 Data quickly available (within 3 to 7 days)\n\u00abReliable to detect differences\n\n\u2018\u00a9 Easily transferable\n\n\u2018Aim\n+ Establishment of assay conditions, \u00a9.g., mainstream smoke concentrations and\nendpoints, for acute inhalation routinely used to detect product modifications\n= Determine the sensitivity of this inhalation assay as indicated by the discrimination\nof various cigarette types\n\nGeneral Design\n\n\u2018\u00a9 This study consists of a series of 1-day inhalation studies which include\n(1) _ the establishment of a dose-response curve for 1R4F Reference Cigarette\n(up to sublethal concentrations of 500 4g TPM)\nand\n(2) _ the use of various cigarette types to show that the chosen end points are\npossibly able to detect product modifications with regard to sensory irritation\nand systemic toxicity;\nin this part of the study, a concentration will be used which will be selected\nfrom the first part of the study.\n\nSbZ989Z90z", "words": [{"text": "INBIFO", "x0": 107, "y0": 108, "x1": 153, "y1": 119, "conf": 82.0}, {"text": "Institut", "x0": 158, "y0": 108, "x1": 199, "y1": 119, "conf": 96.